FAWE-BIM
========

FAWE-BIM ("FastAsyncWorldEdit, but in mods") is an independent port of the
feature set and command surface of FastAsyncWorldEdit and WorldEdit to the
Fabric mod loader for Minecraft 1.21.10, with no plugin or server platform
dependency. It is maintained by MaxLananas.

It reproduces:
  * the WorldEdit 7.3.17 command surface for Minecraft 1.21.10 plus the
    commands FastAsyncWorldEdit adds on top of it,
  * WorldEdit's selection, mask, pattern, transform, brush and tool model,
  * FAWE's data model: palette-packed chunk sections, bulk chunk application,
    deferred "side effects" (lighting, block updates), history recorded per
    chunk section, block change limits and operation timeouts,
  * the schematic formats (Sponge v1/v2/v3, legacy MCEdit .schematic and
    structure .nbt) with their FAWE clipboard semantics.

Reference upstream projects, both licensed GPL-3.0:
  * FastAsyncWorldEdit - https://github.com/IntellectualSites/FastAsyncWorldEdit
      Copyright (C) IntellectualSites and contributors
  * WorldEdit          - https://github.com/EngineHub/WorldEdit
      Copyright (C) sk89q and contributors

The upstream sources were used as the behavioural specification: command names,
aliases, flags, argument lists, parser ids (masks, patterns, transforms), brush
and tool semantics and default configuration values come from them so that FAWE
users find the same commands and the same results. The implementation in this
repository was written for this project; no upstream source file is copied
verbatim, so no upstream file carries over its original authorship. The behaviour
is derived from the GPL-3.0 licensed projects above, and this project is
therefore licensed GPL-3.0 as well (see LICENSE.txt).

Neither FastAsyncWorldEdit nor WorldEdit is required at runtime: the mod ships
its own engine.

FAWE-BIM author and maintainer: MaxLananas.
